Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               meson (>= 0.61),
               pkgconf,
               libglib2.0-dev,
               libgusb-dev,
               libssl-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/TenSeventy7/libfprint-egismoc-sdcp

Package: honor-fmbp-libfprint-sdcp
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: fprintd
Description: SDCP libfprint override for the HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 fingerprint reader
 EgisTec ET171 (1c7a:05aa) support: libfprint 1.94.9 from the
 TenSeventy7/libfprint-egismoc-sdcp fork (SDCP match-on-chip protocol) with
 EvernightFedora's PR #1 device support — 05aa id, SDCP-init command before
 connect, skip of the unsupported USB control-init, 15 enroll stages — plus
 a meson fix so an egismoc-only build links openssl.
 .
 STOPGAP package: the library installs to a private directory
 (/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/honor-fmbp/) and is preferred over the stock
 (SDCP-less) libfprint-2.so.2 purely via ld.so.conf.d ordering — no distro
 file is diverted or held. Remove this package to fall back to stock
 libfprint. Superseded once SDCP support lands in upstream libfprint.
